<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tom Adams</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1931">1931</a>–<a href="/years/1985">1985</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tom Adams (1931–1985) was a Barbadian politician who was prime minister from 1976 until his death in office in 1985. The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grantley-adams">Grantley Adams</a>, the island's first premier, he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbados-labour-party">Barbados Labour Party</a> and backed the United States-led intervention in Grenada in 1983.</p></div>
